  "speakerBios" : {
    "Adam Faughn" : "Married to the former Leah Moon, Adam Faughn has preached for the Central Church of Christ in Paducah, Kentucky since July 2018. He and Leah are blessed with two children, Mary Carol and Turner.\n\nAdam is a graduate of Freed-Hardeman University, having received a B.A. in History (1999) and a Master of Ministry (2003). Prior to working in Paducah, Adam preached in both Nashville, Tennessee and Haleyville, Alabama.\n\nHe has appeared on the Freed-Hardeman Bible lectureship and Polishing the Pulpit, and has held meetings in various states. He and other members of his family contribute to a website—A Legacy of Faith—designed to encourage families.",
    "Bart Warren" : "Bart has been preaching full-time since 2003 and has served congregations in Tennessee and Kentucky (at the South Green Street Church of Christ in Glasgow, KY since 2010). He has taught at preacher training schools in both Tennessee (Southeast Institute of Biblical Studies) and Colorado (Bear Valley Bible Institute). He is Vice-President of Warren Christian Apologetics Center and is the associate editor of an apologetics journal, Sufficient Evidence.\n\nHe is married to Laura (Hanstein), and they have three boys: Ike & Jet (twins) and Jake.",
    "Carla Moore" : "Carla grew up in a family dedicated to ministry, then met John while they were in college at Texas State University. They married in 1986, and have since been involved in ministry at the Bible Chair on the campus of TSU, then with the Southwest School of Bible Studies in Austin and then with the Dripping Springs church of Christ in Dripping Springs, Texas. They currently work with the Bear Valley Bible Institute. Carla taught for more than ten years in the Christian Women's Studies program at the Southwest School of Bible Studies and currently teaches in the women's program at Bear Valley Bible Institute. She enjoys speaking to women of all ages in various places, and is a staff writer for Christian Woman. She is the author of the blog Walking Where Jesus Walked and The Scripture Writing Project.",
    "Glenn Hitchcock" : "Glenn Hitchcock was born in Newport News, Va. He is married to the former Mercedes Dowson (51 years) and they have one daughter, Lauren. The Hitchcocks resided in Hampton, Virginia and are members of the Peninsula church of Christ where Glenn served as one of her elders.\n\nGlenn is a 1982 graduate of the Memphis School of Preaching and a 1988 graduate of Saint Leo College with a B.A. He completed graduate education in 1995 from Norfolk State University School of Social Work. Glenn is a United States honorably discharged Air Force veteran (1972–1980).\n\nSince 1996, Glenn has edited a weekly devotional, \"Thoughts For Today To Brighten Your Day.\" Glenn retired from healthcare in 2019, and he still conducts meetings, marriage seminars and workshops as his schedule permits.",
    "John Moore" : "A native of Dripping Springs, Texas, John has served as an evangelist, teacher, preacher and minister of the gospel for over 30 years. He and his wife Carla are working with Bear Valley Bible Institute International, and serve as the directors of Bible Passages, a ministry dedicated to training preachers, equipping the saints, defending the faith, and guiding souls to Jesus. He is the narrator and author of both the book and video Searching For Truth, and directs the Bible Land Passages Project. Since 1986 John has preached in Gospel Meetings in over eighteen states, and has conducted or participated in yearly campaigns to various foreign countries including Jamaica, Tobago, Malaysia, and Singapore.\n\nJohn and Carla have three sons and five grandchildren.",
    "Kathy Pollard" : "Kathy is married to Neal Pollard, who preaches for the Lehman Ave. church of Christ in Bowling Green, KY. They have three grown sons, all married, and two new grandsons with another grandchild on the way! Kathy attended Faulkner University and Bear Valley Bible Institute and has a bachelor's degree in Bible. She is a writer for Christian Woman magazine, contributes the Bible-marking feature at comefillyourcup.com, and is the author of the book Return to Me…What to Do When Loved Ones Fall Away. She and Carla Moore host a weekly podcast for Christian women called Looking Up. Kathy enjoys spending time with family, traveling to Israel, tending her gardens, and getting to know her new dairy cow, Peaches.",
    "Mike Vestal" : "Mike has served the Westside congregation in Midland, TX for almost 24 years. He and his wife Cherie met at Freed-Hardeman University and they have been married since 1983. They are blessed with 2 children and 4 grandchildren. Their son David preaches for the Lord's church in Mathis, TX. Mike has preached in 37 different states and in 6 foreign countries. He often speaks on brotherhood programs such as PTP and Focal Point. Mike currently serves as an adjunct instructor at Bear Valley Bible Institute in Denver, CO."
  },
